      <ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">1017</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamza-ibn-ali">Hamza ibn Ali</a> begins to preach the Unitarian doctrine in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>, and the divine call is opened</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1018</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> al-Hakim has the preacher al-Darazi executed, leaving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamza-ibn-ali">Hamza ibn Ali</a> the sole leader of the new faith</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1021</span><span class="rf-text">After al-Hakim’s disappearance the regent Sitt al-Mulk orders the army to destroy the movement, opening years of persecution, the mihna</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1043</span><span class="rf-text">Baha al-Din al-Muqtana declares that no new pledges will be accepted, and the faith closes to converts</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1305</span><span class="rf-text">After a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatwa">fatwa</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-taymiyya">Ibn Taymiyya</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-nasir-muhammad">al-Nasir Muhammad</a> inflicts a disastrous defeat on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/druze">Druze</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keserwan">Keserwan</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1635</span><span class="rf-text">The Ottoman sultan has Fakhr-al-Din II killed, the Ma’an emir under whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/druze">Druze</a> dominion had reached from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> plain to Safad</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1711</span><span class="rf-text">The battle of Ain Dara routs the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamani">Yamani</a> faction, and many Yamani <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/druze">Druze</a> migrate from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-lebanon">Mount Lebanon</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hauran">Hauran</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1925–27</span><span class="rf-text">Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-al-atrash">Sultan Pasha al-Atrash</a> the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/druze">Druze</a> provide much of the military force of the Syrian Revolution against French rule</span></li></ol>
